{
  "result": "If I could only change one thing, I wouldn't make everyone richer, smarter, or even healthier - though those would be amazing.\n\nI would give everyone the ability to *truly* understand and feel each other.\n\nNot to read minds or agree on everything, but to have radical, automatic empathy. To for a moment, actually feel what it's like to be the other person - the single mom working two jobs, the kid being bullied at school, the stranger on the other side of the political argument, the refugee, the CEO, the person who hurt you.\n\nBecause I think most of the world's worst problems don't come from a lack of resources or intelligence. We have enough food, enough knowledge, enough solutions for a lot of things. They come from a lack of *felt* understanding. It's easy to ignore hunger, war, cruelty, or the planet itself when it feels distant and abstract. It's almost impossible to ignore it when you feel it in your chest as if it were your own.\n\nIf people couldn't dehumanize each other so easily, I think so much else would fix itself. We wouldn't let children go hungry. We wouldn't be so quick to go to war. We wouldn't destroy the environment we all share. And we wouldn't be so lonely - because we'd finally feel seen.\n\nWe'd still disagree, we'd still be beautifully different, but we'd disagree with compassion instead of contempt.\n\nThat's my one wish - a world where understanding comes before judgment.\n\nWhat about you? What would your one change be?",
